KNOWNBUG
format.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ format: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
could not fully type-check
--
libstdc++ 13 <format>: std::format("{}", 42) returns a nondeterministic
string, so the first assertion fails.  It used to crash (SIGSEGV;
cpp11_partial_specialization_const_T_matching_const_array) and then failed
to convert (cpp11_brace_elision_in_return_and_argument).  Remaining drops:
format:1422 'format' (__formatter_fp::format), 2456 _M_write and
bits/ranges_algobase.h:311 operator() (std::ranges::copy, see
test_ranges_copy.desc).  g++ 13 accepts this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
